claim.claim-text:
a shank (176) extending along an axis (AX) between a proximal end (178) and a distal end (180);
an interface (124) arranged between the proximal end (178) and the distal end (180), the interface (124) comprising at least two outermost drive portions (202) spaced from one another to define a maximum drive dimension of the interface (124) with the two outermost drive portions (202) each separately spaced at a first interface distance (204) from the axis (AX); and
a resilient arm (188) extending from the proximal end (178) of the shank (176) to an arm end (200), the resilient arm (188) comprising an outer arm surface (222) facing away from the axis (AX), and a retention surface (224) facing toward the distal end (180) of the shank (176) and radially aligned about the axis (AX) with one of the outermost drive portions (202), the resilient arm (188) being movable relative to the axis (AX) between:
